window.EDMUND_IELTS_READING_ANALYSIS_CONTENT = Object.freeze({"version":"2026-08-08.2","articles":{"mungo-man":{"id":"mungo-man","catalogueId":"p1-161","passage":1,"title":"Mungo Man","eyebrow":"IELTS Reading · Passage 1","description":"逐題拆解定位、同義改寫、答案證據與常見陷阱。","questionCount":14,"answerKey":["A","E","A","B","C","D","B","A","TRUE","NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE","TRUE","NOT GIVEN"],"questions":[{"number":1,"answer":"A — Jim Bowler","answerKey":"A","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He was searching for ancient lakes when he found the cremated remains of Mungo Lady.”","translation":"他在尋找古代湖泊時，發現了被火化的 Mungo Lady 遺骸。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對題。題目要我們找出「誰」在尋找 ancient lakes 時，發現了 Mungo Lady 的 cremated remains。這類題最重要的是人名和動作的配對：不要只看到 Mungo Lady 就急著選，要看誰做了 finding，以及當時他在做甚麼。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph B"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This treasure trove of history was found by the University of Melbourne geologist Professor Jim Bowler in 1969.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個歷史寶庫是在 1969 年由墨爾本大學地質學教授 Jim Bowler 發現的。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“A comprehensive study of 25 different sediment layers at Lake Mungo concludes that both graves are 40,000 years old.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"一項對 Lake Mungo 二十五個不同沉積層的全面研究得出結論：兩個墓葬都有四萬年歷史。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看第一句和最後一句，可以先猜 Paragraph B 的功能：這段主要交代 Lake Mungo 重要遺骸的發現者、發現年份，以及後來如何估算年代。第一句直接出現 Jim Bowler 和 found，最後一句轉向 dating，所以這段很可能回答和「誰發現 Mungo Lady / Mungo Man」及「年代估算」有關的題目。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目中最有定位力的字是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“searching for ancient lakes”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“cremated remains of Mungo Lady”"},{"kind":"label","text":"掃描 Paragraph B，很快可以找到"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“He was searching for ancient lakes and came across the charred remains of Mungo Lady, who had been cremated.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他當時正在尋找古代湖泊，然後偶然發現了 Mungo Lady 被燒焦的遺骸；她曾被火化。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這一句和題目幾乎完全對應。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句前面先說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This treasure trove of history was found by the University of Melbourne geologist Professor Jim Bowler in 1969.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個歷史寶庫是在 1969 年由墨爾本大學地質學教授 Jim Bowler 發現的。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“He was searching for ancient lakes and came across the charred remains of Mungo Lady, who had been cremated.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他正在尋找古代湖泊時，偶然發現了 Mungo Lady 被燒焦的遺骸；她曾被火化。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這裡的 “He” 指上一句的 Professor Jim Bowler。題目沒有直接給名字，只用 He，所以必須回看代名詞指涉。這裡的 he 不是 Alan Thorne，也不是其他後文學者，而是上一句剛剛提到的 Jim Bowler。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“charred remains” 指燒焦的遺骸。題目把它改寫成 “cremated remains”，因為原文補充 “who had been cremated”，即她曾被火化。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“was searching for ancient lakes”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“was searching for ancient lakes”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這部分幾乎原字重現。"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“found the cremated remains of Mungo Lady”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“came across the charred remains of Mungo Lady, who had been cremated”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"found","to":"came across"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"cremated remains","to":"charred remains + had been cremated"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 A — Jim Bowler。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 “Mungo Lady” 和 “Mungo Man” 在同一段同時出現。原文說 Bowler 在 1969 年發現 Mungo Lady，在 1974 年又發現 Mungo Man。題目問的是 Mungo Lady，且明確說 cremated remains，所以要鎖定 1969 那一句。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是代名詞 “He”。人物配對題常會先給人名，下一句才用 he / his 繼續描述。看到 he 時一定要回看上一句的主語。這題的 he 指 Jim Bowler。"}]}]},{"number":2,"answer":"E — Chris Stringer","answerKey":"E","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He expressed scepticism about the reliability of DNA analysis of the fossils.”","translation":"他對化石 DNA 分析的可靠性表示懷疑。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。題目重點有三個：第一，這個人 expressed scepticism，即表示懷疑；第二，懷疑對象是 DNA analysis；第三，內容和 fossils 有關。掃描時要找和 Out of Africa、DNA sequences、 research community、repeat in other labs 相關的句子。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph D"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“However, Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs because of the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而，支持「走出非洲」理論的人，並不會因為澳洲研究而放棄自己的信念。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In 1997, Pääbo’s research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint from the Feldhofer Neanderthal skeleton uncovered in Germany in 1865—the first Neanderthal remains ever found.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1997 年，Pääbo 的研究團隊從 1865 年在德國發現的 Feldhofer 尼安德塔人骨架中，取得了一個 mtDNA 指紋；那是首批被發現的尼安德塔人遺骸。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以先猜 Paragraph D 的功能：這段處理 DNA 研究、Out of Africa 支持者的反應，以及不同研究者如何解讀澳洲研究。首句已經說 Out of Africa supporters 不會放棄信念，因此中間很可能出現他們對澳洲研究的保留態度。Question 2 說 expressed scepticism，非常可能在這段。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“scepticism”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“reliability”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“DNA analysis”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文中沒有直接用 “scepticism about reliability” 這整句，但有："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Professor Chris Stringer, from the Natural History Museum in London, UK, said that the research community would want to see the work repeated in other labs before major conclusions were drawn from the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"英國倫敦自然歷史博物館的 Chris Stringer 教授說，研究界會希望看到這項工作在其他實驗室重複進行，然後才從澳洲研究中得出重大結論。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“But even assuming the DNA sequences were correct…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"即使假設這些 DNA 序列是正確的……這兩句都顯示他對研究結果保持謹慎態度。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Professor Chris Stringer … said that the research community would want to see the work repeated in other labs before major conclusions were drawn from the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Chris Stringer 教授說，研究界會希望這項工作先在其他實驗室重複，再作出重大結論。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句的核心是 “would want to see the work repeated in other labs”。如果一項研究結果需要在其他實驗室重複驗證，代表說話者不想立刻接受其結論。他不是直接說 “the DNA analysis is wrong”，但他要求 repeated in other labs，這就是對可靠性或可重現性的保留。"},{"kind":"label","text":"另一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“But even assuming the DNA sequences were correct…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"即使假設這些 DNA 序列是正確的……"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“even assuming” 很有態度。它表示：就算先讓一步，暫時假設 DNA 序列無誤，也未必能推出 Thorne 等人想推出的重大結論。這進一步顯示 Stringer 對澳洲 DNA 研究的解讀非常謹慎。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“expressed scepticism about the reliability of DNA analysis”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“would want to see the work repeated in other labs”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“even assuming the DNA sequences were correct”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"expressed scepticism","to":"did not accept the conclusions immediately / wanted replication"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"reliability","to":"whether the work could be repeated and trusted"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"DNA analysis","to":"DNA sequences in the Australian research"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 E — Chris Stringer。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 Rainer Grün。Paragraph F 中 Grün 也說 “doesn’t mean they are absolutely correct”，看起來也像懷疑可靠性。但他談的是 dating results，也就是年代測定資料，並非 DNA analysis。題目明確寫 DNA analysis，所以不能選 Grün。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 Alan Thorne。Thorne 支持 multiregional explanation，且他提出 mitochondrial DNA 應該如何顯示祖先來源。但 Question 2 問的是誰對 DNA 分析可靠性表示懷疑，這一點由 Stringer 的 repeated in other labs 最清楚支持。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“repeated in other labs”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"和"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“DNA sequences”。"}]}]},{"number":3,"answer":"A — Jim Bowler","answerKey":"A","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He dated Mungo Man substantially younger than the previous estimate of 62,000 years.”","translation":"他把 Mungo Man 的年代測定為比之前 62,000 年的估算年輕得多。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。題目重點是 “substantially younger than the previous estimate of 62,000 years”。所以我們要找兩組年代：一組是 62,000 years，另一組是較年輕的年代。然後再看較年輕年代是哪個人或哪個團隊提出。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"主力目標段落：Paragraph B；比較提示在 Paragraph C 開頭。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph B 第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This treasure trove of history was found by the University of Melbourne geologist Professor Jim Bowler in 1969.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個歷史寶庫是在 1969 年由墨爾本大學地質學教授 Jim Bowler 發現的。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph B 最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“A comprehensive study of 25 different sediment layers at Lake Mungo concludes that both graves are 40,000 years old.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"一項對 Lake Mungo 二十五個不同沉積層的全面研究得出結論：兩個墓葬都有四萬年歷史。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph C 第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This is much younger than the age of 62,000 years attributed to Mungo Man in 1999 by a team led by Professor Alan Thorne, of the Australian National University.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這比 1999 年由澳洲國立大學 Alan Thorne 教授帶領的團隊為 Mungo Man 歸定的 62,000 年年齡年輕得多。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Skim 後可以先判斷：Paragraph B 講 Bowler 的發現和 40,000 年年代；Paragraph C 開頭把 40,000 年和 Thorne 的 62,000 年作比較。這正好對應題目中的 “substantially younger than the previous estimate of 62,000 years”。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“younger”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“62,000 years”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“dated”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"掃描 Paragraph C，直接看到 “much younger than the age of 62,000 years”。再回看前一句的 this，就知道 this 指 Paragraph B 最後的 “both graves are 40,000 years old”。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph B 關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“A comprehensive study of 25 different sediment layers at Lake Mungo concludes that both graves are 40,000 years old.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"對 Lake Mungo 25 個沉積層的全面研究得出結論：兩個墓葬都是 40,000 年前的。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph C 接著說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This is much younger than the age of 62,000 years attributed to Mungo Man in 1999 by a team led by Professor Alan Thorne…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個年代比 Alan Thorne 團隊在 1999 年提出的 62,000 年年齡年輕得多。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這裡 “This” 指 40,000 years old。題目說 “substantially younger” 對應原文 “much younger”。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"40,000 與 62,000 相差 22,000 年，所以 “substantially” 合理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"誰提出 40,000 年？Paragraph B 的發現與研究脈絡在 Jim Bowler 之下，而且後文 Paragraph E 、F、G 都反覆提到 “Bowler’s team” 和 “Bowler team’s research”。所以答案是 Jim Bowler。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“dated Mungo Man substantially younger”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“both graves are 40,000 years old”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This is much younger than the age of 62,000 years…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"substantially younger","to":"much younger"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"previous estimate of 62,000 years","to":"age of 62,000 years attributed in 1999 by Thorne’s team"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"dated Mungo Man younger","to":"concluded both graves are 40,000 years old"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 A — Jim Bowler。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 Alan Thorne。題目出現 62,000 years，而 62,000 正是 Thorne 的估算，所以學生可能選 Thorne。但題目問的是「誰把 Mungo Man 定得比 62,000 年年輕很多」。提出 62,000 的人是 Thorne；提出 40,000 年的新研究方向屬於 Bowler 團隊。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 carbon dating 的 28,000 至 32,000 年。Paragraph B 也提到這個初步估算，但題目明確比較 previous estimate of 62,000 years，後文對應的是 40,000 years old，不是 28,000–32,000。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"真正控制答案的是 “This is much younger than…” 中的 this，必須回指 Paragraph B 的 40,000 年研究結論。"}]}]},{"number":4,"answer":"B — Alan Thorne","answerKey":"B","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He said that Mungo Man’s precise age was irrelevant to the debate about human origins.”","translation":"他說 Mungo Man 的精確年齡對人類起源的辯論已經無關緊要。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。題目重點是 “precise age was irrelevant” 和 “debate about human origins”。掃描時要找 irrelevant、doesn’t matter、human origins、40,000 or 60,000 等字眼。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph F"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Thorne counters that Bowler’s team used one dating technique, while he used three.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thorne 反駁說，Bowler 團隊只用了一種年代測定技術，而他用了三種。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“‘So Mungo Man’s ancestors had plenty of time to reach Australia. It doesn’t matter whether he is 40,000 or 60,000 years old.’”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"「所以 Mungo Man 的祖先有充足時間到達澳洲。他到底是 40,000 年還是 60,000 年歷史，已經不重要。」只看首尾句，可以猜 Paragraph F 的功能：這段先呈現 Thorne 對 Bowler 年代測定方法的反駁，後面再說他對 Mungo Man 年齡與人類起源辯論的最新看法。最後一句和題目非常接近。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“irrelevant”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“human origins”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“precise age”"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph F 中直接有"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Now, however, Thorne says the age of Mungo Man is irrelevant to this debate about human origins.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而現在，Thorne 說 Mungo Man 的年齡對這場人類起源辯論已經無關緊要。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句幾乎就是題目的來源。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Now, however, Thorne says the age of Mungo Man is irrelevant to this debate about human origins.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而現在，Thorne 說 Mungo Man 的年齡對這場人類起源辯論已經無關緊要。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這一句直接給出答案。主語是 Thorne，動詞是 says，內容是 age of Mungo Man is irrelevant。"},{"kind":"label","text":"後面他解釋原因"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Recent fossil finds show that modern humans were in China 110,000 years ago.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"最近的化石發現顯示，現代人類在 110,000 年前已經在中國出現。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“So Mungo Man’s ancestors had plenty of time to reach Australia. It doesn’t matter whether he is 40,000 or 60,000 years old.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以 Mungo Man 的祖先有足夠時間到達澳洲。無論他是 40,000 年還是 60,000 年歷史，都不重要。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這裡 “doesn’t matter” 就是題目的 “irrelevant”。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man’s precise age was irrelevant”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“the age of Mungo Man is irrelevant”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“It doesn’t matter whether he is 40,000 or 60,000 years old”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"precise age","to":"whether he is 40,000 or 60,000 years old"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"irrelevant","to":"doesn’t matter"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"debate about human origins","to":"this debate about human origins"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 B — Alan Thorne。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 Bowler 也一直參與年代爭論，而且 Paragraph F 開頭提到 Bowler’s team。可是題目中的原句 “the age of Mungo Man is irrelevant…” 明確以 Thorne 為主語。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 “human origins”。這個詞在 Paragraph C 也出現，因為 Thorne 支持 multiregional explanation，反對 Out of Africa theory。學生若只按主題定位到 C，仍要繼續掃描到 Paragraph F，因為 “irrelevant” 這個態度詞在 F 段才出現。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Thorne says…”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"和"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“doesn’t matter”。"}]}]},{"number":5,"answer":"C — Svante Pääbo","answerKey":"C","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“His research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint from the first Neanderthal remains found in Europe.”","translation":"他的研究團隊從歐洲首次發現的尼安德塔人遺骸中取得 mtDNA 指紋。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。題目中最強的定位詞是 mtDNA fingerprint 和 Neanderthal。這類專有名詞非常容易定位，通常比一般詞如 research group 更有用。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph D"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“However, Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs because of the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而，支持「走出非洲」理論的人，並不會因澳洲研究而放棄自己的信念。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In 1997, Pääbo’s research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint from the Feldhofer Neanderthal skeleton uncovered in Germany in 1865—the first Neanderthal remains ever found.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1997 年，Pääbo 的研究團隊從 1865 年在德國發現的 Feldhofer 尼安德塔人骨架中取得 mtDNA 指紋；那是有史以來首次被發現的尼安德塔人遺骸。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以看出 Paragraph D 主要處理 DNA、Out of Africa 相關爭論，以及某些基因研究證據。最後一句直接出現 Pääbo、mtDNA fingerprint 和 Neanderthal skeleton，因此 Question 5 幾乎可直接定位到段末。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“mtDNA fingerprint”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Neanderthal remains”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文段末直接有"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Pääbo’s research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint…”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這是完整對應。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In 1997, Pääbo’s research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint from the Feldhofer Neanderthal skeleton uncovered in Germany in 1865—the first Neanderthal remains ever found.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1997 年，Pääbo 的研究團隊從 1865 年在德國發現的 Feldhofer 尼安德塔人骨架中取得 mtDNA 指紋；那是有史以來首次被發現的尼安德塔人遺骸。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句中的 “Pääbo’s research group” 對應題目 “His research group”。選項中 C 是 Svante Pääbo ，所以答案是 C。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“recovered an mtDNA fingerprint” 幾乎與題目原字相同。“the first Neanderthal remains ever found” 題目改寫成 “the first Neanderthal remains found in Europe”。原文說該骨架在 Germany 發現，Germany 在 Europe，所以題目的 “in Europe” 是地理概括。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“His research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Pääbo’s research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint”"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“from the first Neanderthal remains found in Europe”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“from the Feldhofer Neanderthal skeleton uncovered in Germany in 1865—the first Neanderthal remains ever found”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"His research group","to":"Pääbo’s research group"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"found in Europe","to":"uncovered in Germany"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"first Neanderthal remains","to":"first Neanderthal remains ever found"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 C — Svante Pääbo。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是選項中沒有只寫 Pääbo，完整名字是 Svante Pääbo。原文只出現姓氏 Pääbo，但人物配對表的 C 正是 Svante Pääbo。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 Paragraph D 前半主要講 Chris Stringer。學生若只看段落開頭，可能以為整段都只關於 Stringer。可是段落最後換到 Pääbo’s research group，所以要看題目定位詞。mtDNA fingerprint 是最強訊號。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第三個中伏位是 “first Neanderthal remains found in Europe”。原文說 Germany，不直接寫 Europe。這裡是上位地理概括：Germany 屬於 Europe，所以可以對應。"}]}]},{"number":6,"answer":"D — Tim Flannery","answerKey":"D","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He supports the idea that hunting by early humans caused Australia’s megafauna to become extinct.”","translation":"他支持這個看法：早期人類的狩獵導致澳洲巨型動物滅絕。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。題目核心是 hunting by early humans 和 megafauna became extinct。掃描時要找 megafauna、hunting、blitzkrieg、arriving people、extinction 等詞。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph G"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Tim Flannery, a proponent of the controversial theory that Australia’s megafauna were wiped out 46,000 years ago in a ‘blitzkrieg’ of hunting by the arriving people, also claims the new Mungo dates support this view.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Tim Flannery 博士支持一個具爭議性的理論：澳洲巨型動物在 46,000 年前被抵達的人類以「閃電戰」式狩獵消滅；他也聲稱新的 Mungo 年代支持這個看法。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“‘It’s my view that humans arrived and extinction took place in almost the same geological instant.’”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"「我的看法是，人類抵達和動物滅絕幾乎發生在同一個地質瞬間。」只看第一句和最後一句，可以猜 Paragraph G 的功能：這段介紹 Tim Flannery 的 megafauna extinction 理論。他認為人類到達與巨型動物滅絕時間非常接近，並把狩獵視為關鍵原因。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“hunting”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“megafauna”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“extinct”"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph G 第一行已經有"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“megafauna were wiped out … in a ‘blitzkrieg’ of hunting by the arriving people”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"巨型動物被抵達的人類以「閃電戰」式狩獵消滅。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這就是題目的直接來源。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Tim Flannery, a proponent of the controversial theory that Australia’s megafauna were wiped out 46,000 years ago in a ‘blitzkrieg’ of hunting by the arriving people…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Tim Flannery 博士是一個具爭議理論的支持者；該理論認為澳洲巨型動物在 46,000 年前被抵達的人類以密集狩獵方式消滅。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“a proponent of” 指支持者。“megafauna were wiped out” 指巨型動物被消滅、滅絕。“hunting by the arriving people” 對應題目 “hunting by early humans”。段落最後一句也加強這點：“humans arrived and extinction took place in almost the same geological instant”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"人類到達和滅絕幾乎在同一個地質瞬間發生。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這說明 Flannery 把人類到達和滅絕事件緊密連接起來。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“supports the idea”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“a proponent of the controversial theory”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"supports","to":"is a proponent of"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“hunting by early humans caused Australia’s megafauna to become extinct”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Australia’s megafauna were wiped out … in a ‘blitzkrieg’ of hunting by the arriving people”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"early humans","to":"arriving people"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"became extinct","to":"were wiped out"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"hunting caused extinction","to":"wiped out in a blitzkrieg of hunting"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 D — Tim Flannery。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 Jim Bowler 也在 G 段被提到，因為 Flannery praises the Bowler team’s research。可是題目問支持 hunting extinction theory 的人；原文第一句直接說 Tim Flannery 是該 theory 的 proponent。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 “new Mungo dates support this view”。學生可能把 support this view 的動作放到 Bowler team 身上。其實是 Flannery claims the new dates support this view。Bowler 本人到 Paragraph H 反而對 Flannery 的理論表示懷疑。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Tim Flannery, a proponent of…”。"}]}]},{"number":7,"answer":"B — Alan Thorne","answerKey":"B","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He proposed a multiregional explanation instead of a single place of origin.”","translation":"他提出多地區起源解釋，而非單一起源地的說法。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。定位詞非常明顯：multiregional explanation 和 single place of origin。這兩個詞和人類起源理論有關，應在談 Out of Africa theory 的段落。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph C"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This is much younger than the age of 62,000 years attributed to Mungo Man in 1999 by a team led by Professor Alan Thorne, of the Australian National University.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這比 1999 年由澳洲國立大學 Alan Thorne 教授帶領團隊為 Mungo Man 歸定的 62,000 年年齡年輕得多。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“If Mungo Man were descended from ancestors who had left Africa within the past 200,000 years, Thorne argues, then his mitochondrial DNA should have looked like that of the other samples.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thorne 認為，如果 Mungo Man 是過去 200,000 年內離開非洲的祖先的後代，那麼他的線粒體 DNA 應該會看起來像其他樣本。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以猜 Paragraph C 的功能：這段先引入 Alan Thorne 的 62,000 年估算，然後轉入他對人類起源的理論立場，尤其是他如何用 mitochondrial DNA 和 Out of Africa 理論作比較。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Question 7 的 multiregional explanation 明顯會在這裡。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“multiregional explanation”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“single place of origin”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文中有兩句直接對應"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Thorne is the country’s leading opponent of the Out of Africa theory—the idea that Homo sapiens had a single place of origin.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thorne 是澳洲國內最主要的「走出非洲」理論反對者；該理論認為 Homo sapiens 有單一起源地。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Alan Thorne supports the multiregional explanation…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Alan Thorne 博士支持多地區解釋。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Thorne is the country’s leading opponent of the Out of Africa theory—the idea that Homo sapiens had a single place of origin.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thorne 是該國最主要的 Out of Africa 理論反對者；這個理論認為 Homo sapiens 有單一起源地。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句先定義 Out of Africa theory：Homo sapiens had a single place of origin。題目中的 “single place of origin” 直接來自這句。"},{"kind":"label","text":"下一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Alan Thorne supports the multiregional explanation: modern humans arose simultaneously in Africa, Europe and Asia from one of our predecessors, Homo erectus…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Alan Thorne 博士支持多地區解釋：現代人類是由我們的祖先之一 Homo erectus 在非洲、歐洲和亞洲同時演化而來。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句直接說 Thorne supports the multiregional explanation。因此答案是 Alan Thorne。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“proposed a multiregional explanation”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Alan Thorne supports the multiregional explanation”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"proposed / supports","to":"advocates / accepts this explanation"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“instead of a single place of origin”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“opponent of the Out of Africa theory—the idea that Homo sapiens had a single place of origin”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"single place of origin","to":"Out of Africa theory"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"instead of","to":"opponent of Out of Africa + supports multiregional explanation"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 B — Alan Thorne。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 Chris Stringer。Paragraph D 中 Stringer 支持 Out of Africa 的方向，說 “It’s much more likely that modern humans came out of Africa.” 這與 multiregional explanation 方向不同。題目問提出多地區解釋的人，所以不能選 Stringer。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 Bowler。Bowler 是發現和年代研究的重要人物，但 Paragraph D 說他覺得這些起源辯論是 “irritating, speculative distractions”。他並非 multiregional explanation 的提出者。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Alan Thorne supports the multiregional explanation”。"}]}]},{"number":8,"answer":"A — Jim Bowler","answerKey":"A","type":"人物配對","prompt":"“He argued that climate change, rather than prehistoric human activity, contributed to the megafauna’s extinction.”","translation":"他認為氣候變化，而非史前人類活動，促成了巨型動物的滅絕。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是人物配對。題目重點是 climate change 和 megafauna’s extinction。它和 Question 6 的 Flannery 理論形成對照：Flannery 強調 humans / hunting；這題要找強調 climate change 的人。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph H"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Bowler, however, is sceptical of Flannery’s theory and says the Mungo study provides no definitive new evidence to support it.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而，Bowler 對 Flannery 的理論表示懷疑，並說 Mungo 研究沒有提供明確的新證據來支持該理論。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“‘To blame the earliest Australians for their complete extinction is drawing a longbow.’”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"「把牠們的完全滅絕歸咎於最早期澳洲人，是牽強附會。」只看首尾句，可以猜 Paragraph H 的功能：這段呈現 Bowler 對 Flannery 狩獵滅絕理論的反對或保留。第一句說他 sceptical，最後一句說責怪最早期澳洲人很牽強。因此這段應回答和 climate change / human responsibility / megafauna extinction 有關的題目。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“climate change”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“megafauna’s extinction”"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph H 中有"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“He argues that climate change around 40,000 years ago was more intense than had been previously realised and could have played a role in the megafauna’s demise.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他認為，約 40,000 年前的氣候變化比以往所認識的更劇烈，並可能在巨型動物的滅亡中扮演角色。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句直接給出答案。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“He argues that climate change around 40,000 years ago was more intense than had been previously realised and could have played a role in the megafauna’s demise.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他認為，約 40,000 年前的氣候變化比之前人們認識到的更強烈，並可能在巨型動物滅亡中發揮作用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句主語是 He，而上一句主語是 Bowler，所以 he 指 Jim Bowler。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“climate change” 原文和題目直接一致。“could have played a role” 對應題目 “contributed to”。“megafauna’s demise” 對應 “megafauna’s extinction”。最後一句：“To blame the earliest Australians for their complete extinction is drawing a longbow.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"把牠們的完全滅絕歸咎於最早期澳洲人，是過度牽強的說法。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“drawing a longbow” 是習語，意思是誇大、牽強、過度推斷。這說明 Bowler 對「人類造成完全滅絕」的說法不接受。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“climate change … contributed to the megafauna’s extinction”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“climate change … could have played a role in the megafauna’s demise”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"contributed to","to":"played a role in"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"extinction","to":"demise"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"prehistoric human activity","to":"earliest Australians / hunting by arriving people"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 A — Jim Bowler。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 Tim Flannery。G 段說 Flannery 認為 humans arrived and extinction took place almost together，所以他會支持人類狩獵解釋。H 段開頭用 “however” 轉向 Bowler 的懷疑態度。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個 however 是關鍵轉折。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是題目用了 “rather than prehistoric human activity”。原文沒有逐字說 rather than，但它先說 Bowler is sceptical of Flannery’s theory，再說 climate change could have played a role ，最後說 blaming earliest Australians is drawing a longbow。三句合起來支持題目中的對比方向。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Bowler, however, is sceptical…”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"和"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“climate change … could have played a role”。"}]}]},{"number":9,"answer":"TRUE","answerKey":"TRUE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“The Lake Mungo remains provide archaeologists with vivid evidence of human activity in the area.”","translation":"Lake Mungo 的遺骸為考古學家提供了該地區人類活動的鮮明證據。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN。題目要判斷 Lake Mungo remains 是否提供了關於該地區人類活動的 vivid evidence。重點詞是 remains、archaeologists、story / evidence、human activity 。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph A"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Fifty thousand years ago, a lush landscape greeted the first Australians making their way towards the south-east of the continent.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"五萬年前，一片茂盛的景觀迎接了向澳洲大陸東南方前進的第一批澳洲人。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man is the oldest known example in the world of such a ritual.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Man 是世界上已知最古老的這類儀式例子。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以猜 Paragraph A 的功能：這段先描寫早期澳洲人的環境，再透過 Mungo Man 的身體狀況、生活方式、工具使用痕跡和埋葬方式，重建早期人類活動。最後一句把 Mungo Man 的 burial ritual 放到全球考古意義中。因此 Question 9 很可能來自這段。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“remains”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“archaeologists”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“human activity”"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph A 有一句非常直接"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Together, the three prominent sets of remains found at Lake Mungo tell archaeologists a story about early Australians.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Lake Mungo 發現的三組重要遺骸，合起來向考古學家講述了一個關於早期澳洲人的故事。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句直接對應 archaeologists 和 remains。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Together, the three prominent sets of remains found at Lake Mungo tell archaeologists a story about early Australians.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Lake Mungo 發現的三組重要遺骸，合起來向考古學家講述了一個關於早期澳洲人的故事。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“tell archaeologists a story” 是比喻，意思是這些遺骸提供足夠線索，讓考古學家重建早期澳洲人的生活。後文具體展示這個 “story”：“Mungo Man lived around the shores of the lake with his family.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Man 和家人住在湖邊。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“When he was young, Mungo Man lost his two lower canine teeth, possibly knocked out in a ritual.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他年輕時失去了兩顆下犬齒，可能是在儀式中被敲掉。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Over the years his molar teeth became worn and scratched…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"多年下來，他的臼齒變得磨損和刮花。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Such wear and tear is typical of people who have used a woomera to throw spears over many years.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這種磨損很典型，常見於多年使用 woomera 投擲長矛的人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這些資訊都屬於 human activity：居住、飲食、製作繩索、狩獵、儀式、埋葬。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“provide archaeologists with vivid evidence of human activity”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“tell archaeologists a story about early Australians”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"provide evidence","to":"tell archaeologists a story"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"human activity in the area","to":"lived around the shores, used woomera, ritual tooth removal, burial ritual"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"vivid evidence","to":"detailed clues about life, health, tools and rituals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 TRUE。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案判斷原文不只說有遺骸，還利用遺骸描述 Mungo Man 的生活、年齡、健康、飲食、工具使用和葬禮。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目中的 “vivid evidence” 是對這些細節的合理概括。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 “vivid” 這個字。原文沒有直接用 vivid，但整段提供很多具體生活細節，所以 vivid 是概括，不要求原字重現。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 “human activity”。有學生可能覺得 remains 只是屍骨，不算活動證據。可是考古學上，骨骼磨損、牙齒狀況、埋葬姿勢和 red ochre 都能揭示生活和文化活動。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“tell archaeologists a story about early Australians”。"}]}]},{"number":10,"answer":"NOT GIVEN","answerKey":"NOT GIVEN","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Weapons used by Mungo Man were found among the Lake Mungo remains.”","translation":"Mungo Man 使用過的武器在 Lake Mungo 遺骸之中被發現。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN。題目有兩個核心部分：第一，Mungo Man used weapons；"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二，weapons were found among the remains。原文若只說他可能使用過武器，仍未必能支持「武器被發現」。我們要非常小心區分「從身體痕跡推斷使用工具」和「實物武器出土」。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph A"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Fifty thousand years ago, a lush landscape greeted the first Australians making their way towards the south-east of the continent.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"五萬年前，一片茂盛的景觀迎接了向澳洲大陸東南方前進的第一批澳洲人。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man is the oldest known example in the world of such a ritual.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Man 是世界上已知最古老的這類儀式例子。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以先猜 Paragraph A 的功能：這段講早期澳洲人的生活環境，並根據 Mungo Man 的身體遺骸推測他的生活方式和文化活動。題目提到 weapons 和 remains，所以應在這段找與 woomera、spears、bones 等內容相關的句子。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Weapons”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“remains”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文沒有直接用 weapons，但有與武器相關的句子"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Such wear and tear is typical of people who have used a woomera to throw spears over many years.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這種磨損很典型，常見於多年使用 woomera 投擲長矛的人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句提到 woomera 和 spears，最接近題目中的 weapons。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文相關句前面先說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“As Mungo Man grew older his bones ached with arthritis, especially his right elbow, which was so damaged that bits of bone were completely worn out or broken away.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"隨著 Mungo Man 年紀漸長，他的骨頭因關節炎而疼痛，尤其是右手肘，損傷嚴重到有些骨頭完全磨蝕或碎裂。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Such wear and tear is typical of people who have used a woomera to throw spears over many years.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這種磨損常見於多年使用 woomera 投擲長矛的人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這兩句提供的是身體磨損證據。考古學家從他的右手肘損傷推測，他可能長期使用 woomera 投擲長矛。可是題目說 weapons were found among the remains，這是另一種資料：它要求文章說明實物武器出土。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文沒有說找到 woomera，也沒有說找到 spears。它只說骨骼磨損 typical of people who have used a woomera。這可以支持「他可能使用過投矛器或長矛」這個推斷，但不能支持「武器被發現」。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"同義與資料缺失"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目需要"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"weapons used by Mungo Man ● were found ● among the Lake Mungo remains"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文提供"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"right elbow damaged ● wear and tear typical of people using a woomera ● spears mentioned as what woomera throws"},{"kind":"label","text":"缺失部分"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● actual weapons found；"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● weapons among the remains；"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● any statement that a woomera or spears were excavated."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 NOT GIVEN。"}]},{"id":"why-not","title":"為甚麼不是 FALSE","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題最容易出現判斷失誤。原文沒有說武器被發現，但也沒有明確說「沒有任何武器被發現」。因此較嚴格的 IELTS 判斷是 NOT GIVEN。原文只是把武器使用作為從骨骼磨損推斷出的可能性，沒有交代出土物中是否包括武器。"},{"kind":"label","text":"若文章寫"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“No weapons were found with the remains.”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"那才會是 FALSE。現在文章沒有這句，也沒有等同意思。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 “woomera” 和 “spears”。學生看到這兩個武器相關詞，可能會以為武器出土。細讀時要看動詞：原文動詞是 “have used”，證據來源是 “wear and tear”；題目動詞是 “were found”。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"兩者不同。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 “remains”。文章主要說 human remains，即骨骼和相關葬禮痕跡。題目把 weapons 加入 remains 之中，這項內容原文沒有提供。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"真正控制答案的是 found 這個動詞。原文沒有說 weapons were found，所以不能選 TRUE；原文也沒有明確排除武器出土，所以答案是 NOT GIVEN。"}]}]},{"number":11,"answer":"TRUE","answerKey":"TRUE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Mungo Man is the world’s oldest known archaeological evidence of a burial ritual of this kind.”","translation":"Mungo Man 是世界上已知最古老的這類葬禮儀式考古證據。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN。題目重點是 world’s oldest known、burial ritual、of this kind。掃描時要找 oldest known、ritual、buried、red ochre 等詞。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph A"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Fifty thousand years ago, a lush landscape greeted the first Australians making their way towards the south-east of the continent.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"五萬年前，一片茂盛的景觀迎接了向澳洲大陸東南方前進的第一批澳洲人。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man is the oldest known example in the world of such a ritual.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Man 是世界上已知最古老的這類儀式例子。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以直接猜到 Paragraph A 會先重建早期澳洲人的生活，最後落到 Mungo Man 的 burial ritual 的世界考古意義。Question 11 幾乎直接對應最後一句。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“world’s oldest known”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“burial ritual”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文段末有"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man is the oldest known example in the world of such a ritual.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Man 是世界上已知最古老的這類儀式例子。"},{"kind":"label","text":"這句之前則描述 ritual 內容"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“His family mourned him and carefully buried him in the lunette, laying him on his back with his hands crossed in his lap and sprinkling him with red ochre.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他的家人哀悼他，並小心地把他埋葬在新月形沙丘中，讓他仰臥，雙手交疊放在膝上，並在他身上撒上紅赭石。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句一"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“His family mourned him and carefully buried him…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他的家人哀悼他，並小心地埋葬他。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這說明它是 burial，且包含哀悼和精心安排。"},{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句二"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“laying him on his back with his hands crossed in his lap and sprinkling him with red ochre”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"讓他仰臥，雙手交疊放在膝上，並撒上紅赭石。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這些都是 ritual 的具體形式：姿勢、手的位置、red ochre 都不是隨便處理屍體，而是具文化意義的葬禮行為。"},{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句三"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man is the oldest known example in the world of such a ritual.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Man 是世界上已知最古老的這類儀式例子。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目說 “world’s oldest known archaeological evidence of a burial ritual of this kind”。這是對原文的概括。原文的 “example” 指考古上可見的例子；題目用 “archaeological evidence” 讓意思更明確。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“world’s oldest known archaeological evidence”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“the oldest known example in the world”"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“of a burial ritual of this kind”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“such a ritual” referring to careful burial with crossed hands and red ochre"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"oldest known in the world","to":"world’s oldest known"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"example","to":"archaeological evidence / example"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"burial ritual","to":"carefully buried + red ochre + body position"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 TRUE。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 “of this kind”。題目不是說所有 burial 的最早證據，而是這類 ritual 的最早已知例子。這與原文 “such a ritual” 範圍一致。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 red ochre。這不是裝飾性細節，它幫助證明 burial 具有儀式性。題目中的 burial ritual 要靠 “carefully buried”、“hands crossed” 和 “red ochre” 一起支持。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“oldest known example in the world of such a ritual”。"}]}]},{"number":12,"answer":"FALSE","answerKey":"FALSE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“The skeletons of Mungo Man and Mungo Lady were uncovered in the same year.”","translation":"Mungo Man 和 Mungo Lady 的骨骸是在同一年被發現的。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN。題目要求比較兩個發現年份：Mungo Lady 和 Mungo Man 是否同一年被發現。掃描時要找年份 1969、1974，以及 found / uncovered。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph B"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This treasure trove of history was found by the University of Melbourne geologist Professor Jim Bowler in 1969.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個歷史寶庫是在 1969 年由墨爾本大學地質學教授 Jim Bowler 發現的。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“A comprehensive study of 25 different sediment layers at Lake Mungo concludes that both graves are 40,000 years old.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"一項對 Lake Mungo 二十五個不同沉積層的全面研究得出結論：兩個墓葬都有四萬年歷史。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Skim 後可以看出，Paragraph B 既講發現年份，也講年代測定。Question 12 問 same year，所以目標是段落中關於 1969 和 1974 的句子。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Man”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Mungo Lady”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“same year”"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph B 有兩句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“He was searching for ancient lakes and came across the charred remains of Mungo Lady, who had been cremated.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"他在尋找古代湖泊時，發現了被燒焦的 Mungo Lady 遺骸；她曾被火化。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In 1974, he found a second complete skeleton, Mungo Man, buried 300 metres away.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1974 年，他在 300 米外發現了第二具完整骨架，即 Mungo Man。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"而 Paragraph B 第一行已經提供 Mungo Lady 的發現年份：1969。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文先說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This treasure trove of history was found by … Professor Jim Bowler in 1969.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這個歷史寶庫由 Jim Bowler 教授在 1969 年發現。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"接著說他在尋找古代湖泊時發現 Mungo Lady。這表示 Mungo Lady 的發現和 1969 年相連。"},{"kind":"label","text":"然後"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In 1974, he found a second complete skeleton, Mungo Man, buried 300 metres away.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1974 年，他在 300 米外發現了第二具完整骨架 Mungo Man。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目說 two skeletons were uncovered in the same year。原文給出的年份不同： Mungo Lady：1969 Mungo Man：1974 所以題目和原文資訊相反。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"同義與反向關係"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“were uncovered in the same year”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Mungo Lady found in 1969 Mungo Man found in 1974"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"uncovered","to":"found / came across"},{"kind":"label","text":"但時間關係相反"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"same year ↔ 1969 and 1974 所以答案是 FALSE。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 “both graves are 40,000 years old”。學生可能看到 both graves 就覺得兩者時間相同。可是那是墓葬年代，即遺骸本身的古老程度；題目問 uncovered in the same year，即現代考古發現年份。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 Mungo Lady 的遺骸被稱為 “charred remains” 而 Mungo Man 被稱為 “complete skeleton”。題目用 “skeletons” 概括兩者，雖然 Mungo Lady 的表述略不同，但真正決定答案的是年份差異。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1969 和 1974。"}]}]},{"number":13,"answer":"TRUE","answerKey":"TRUE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Scientists disagree about the origins of the earliest Homo sapiens.”","translation":"科學家對最早 Homo sapiens 的起源存在分歧。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN。題目問 scientists 是否 disagree about origins。掃描時要找 Out of Africa theory、single place of origin、multiregional explanation、supporters、opponent 等詞。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph C 和 Paragraph D"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph C 第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“This is much younger than the age of 62,000 years attributed to Mungo Man in 1999 by a team led by Professor Alan Thorne…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這比 Alan Thorne 團隊在 1999 年為 Mungo Man 歸定的 62,000 年年齡年輕得多。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph C 最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“If Mungo Man were descended from ancestors who had left Africa within the past 200,000 years, Thorne argues, then his mitochondrial DNA should have looked like that of the other samples.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thorne 認為，如果 Mungo Man 是過去 200,000 年內離開非洲的祖先後代，那麼他的線粒體 DNA 應該會像其他樣本。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph D 第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“However, Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs because of the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而，支持 Out of Africa 理論的人並不會因澳洲研究而放棄信念。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Skim 後可以猜到：C 段介紹 Thorne 的 multiregional 立場，D 段介紹 Out of Africa 支持者的反應。兩段合起來正是科學界在人類起源問題上的分歧。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“origins”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Homo sapiens”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“disagree”"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph C 有"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“the Out of Africa theory—the idea that Homo sapiens had a single place of origin.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Out of Africa 理論，即 Homo sapiens 有單一起源地的想法。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Dr Alan Thorne supports the multiregional explanation…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Alan Thorne 博士支持多地區解釋。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這已經顯示兩種不同起源理論。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"原文先說 Thorne 是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“the country’s leading opponent of the Out of Africa theory”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"澳洲國內最主要的 Out of Africa 理論反對者。"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“opponent” 表示反對者。這說明科學家之間存在理論分歧。 Out of Africa theory 是：“the idea that Homo sapiens had a single place of origin”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Homo sapiens 有單一起源地的想法。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著，Thorne 的立場是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“modern humans arose simultaneously in Africa, Europe and Asia…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"現代人類在非洲、歐洲和亞洲同時出現。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這就是 multiregional explanation。兩者的核心差異很清楚："},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Out of Africa：單一起源地。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Multiregional：多地區同時演化。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph D 又說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Out of Africa 支持者不準備放棄自己的信念。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這進一步顯示雙方仍有分歧。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Scientists disagree about the origins of the earliest Homo sapiens”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“opponent of the Out of Africa theory”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“supports the multiregional explanation”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫關係"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"scientists disagree","to":"some support Out of Africa; Thorne opposes it and supports multiregional explanation"},{"kind":"comparison","from":"origins of Homo sapiens","to":"single place of origin vs simultaneously in Africa, Europe and Asia"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 TRUE。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是題目用 “scientists” 這個概括詞。原文具體提到 Thorne、Stringer 和 Out of Africa supporters。這些都是研究者或科學界人士，因此可以概括為 scientists。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 “earliest Homo sapiens”。原文說 Homo sapiens had a single place of origin，又說 modern humans arose simultaneously。這裡討論的是現代人類的起源問題，與題目的 origins 對應。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正控制答案的是理論對立"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"single place of origin 對比 multiregional explanation。"}]}]},{"number":14,"answer":"NOT GIVEN","answerKey":"NOT GIVEN","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Supporters of the Out of Africa theory criticised the Australian researchers for using an outdated research method.”","translation":"Out of Africa 理論的支持者批評澳洲研究者使用過時的研究方法。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN。題目有幾個核心部分：Out of Africa supporters、criticised Australian researchers、using an outdated research method。原文若只說他們不同意結論或要求重複實驗，仍不足以支持「批評方法過時」。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph D"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“However, Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs because of the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"然而，Out of Africa 理論支持者並不會因澳洲研究而放棄自己的信念。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In 1997, Pääbo’s research group recovered an mtDNA fingerprint from the Feldhofer Neanderthal skeleton uncovered in Germany in 1865—the first Neanderthal remains ever found.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1997 年，Pääbo 的研究團隊從 1865 年在德國發現的 Feldhofer 尼安德塔人骨架中取得 mtDNA 指紋；那是有史以來首次被發現的尼安德塔人遺骸。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以猜 Paragraph D 會處理 Out of Africa 支持者對澳洲研究的反應，以及 DNA 研究如何影響這場爭論。Question 14 明確提到 Out of Africa supporters，所以定位在 D 段。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目定位詞"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Out of Africa supporters”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“criticised”"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“outdated research method”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文找到"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Professor Chris Stringer … said that the research community would want to see the work repeated in other labs before major conclusions were drawn from the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Chris Stringer 教授說，研究界希望在得出重大結論前，看到這項工作在其他實驗室被重複。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句顯示他們對澳洲研究保持謹慎，要求 replication。可是原文沒有 “outdated method” 的意思。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"關鍵句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Out of Africa supporters are not about to abandon their beliefs because of the Australian research.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Out of Africa 支持者不會因澳洲研究而放棄自己的信念。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句只說他們不接受澳洲研究足以推翻自己的理論。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著 Stringer 說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“the research community would want to see the work repeated in other labs before major conclusions were drawn”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"研究界希望先看到這項工作在其他實驗室重複，再作出重大結論。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這表示他關心研究是否可重複、結果是否穩固。它可以支持「他對研究結論保留」，也可以支持「他想要更多驗證」。可是題目說的是另一件事："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“using an outdated research method”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"使用過時的研究方法。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文沒有提到 outdated、old-fashioned、obsolete、out of date、method was no longer accepted，也沒有說澳洲研究者的方法落後。它只是說結果需要其他實驗室重複。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"同義與資料缺失"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目需要"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Out of Africa supporters ● criticised Australian researchers ● reason: outdated research method"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文提供"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Out of Africa supporters not abandoning beliefs ● Stringer wants work repeated in other labs ● even assuming DNA sequences correct, conclusion may differ"},{"kind":"label","text":"缺失部分"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● explicit criticism of method；"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● outdated method；"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● any comparison between old and modern methods；"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"● any claim that Australian researchers used obsolete techniques。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以答案是 NOT GIVEN。"}]},{"id":"why-not","title":"為甚麼不是 FALSE","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文沒有說澳洲研究方法很新，也沒有說 Out of Africa 支持者沒有批評方法。它只是沒有提供以下資訊："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“outdated research method”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"因此答案應是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"kind":"label","text":"若原文寫"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Stringer said the method was modern and reliable.”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"那才可能反駁題目。現在文章只說需要重複驗證，沒有評論方法是否過時。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第一個中伏位是 “repeated in other labs”。學生可能把「需要重複驗證」理解成「研究方法有問題」。這是可能的科學保留態度，但不等於 outdated method。要保持原文邊界。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"第二個中伏位是 “Australian research”。題目和原文都提到澳洲研究，所以位置正確；但位置正確不代表整句成立。題目加入了 “outdated research method”，原文沒有支援這項資料。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"真正控制答案的是 “outdated”。文章沒有任何同義表達，所以答案是 NOT GIVEN。"}]}]}]},"if-you-can-get-used-to-the-taste":{"id":"if-you-can-get-used-to-the-taste","catalogueId":"p1-092","passage":1,"title":"If You Can Get Used to the Taste","eyebrow":"IELTS Reading · Passage 1","description":"先以七段 Skim Roadmap 建立全篇地圖，再逐題拆解定位、細讀證據、同義改寫及中伏位。","questionCount":13,"answerKey":["FALSE","TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN","calcium","Thailand","indigenous Africans","mopane leaves","southern China","arachnids","D","A","D"],"paragraphOverview":{"title":"Skim Roadmap：全篇段落速覽","intro":"先只看每段第一句和最後一句，建立文章的粗略地圖；完成後才由 Question 1 開始逐題分析。","paragraphs":[{"number":1,"summary":"首句用正式詞 “entomophagy” 開場，說明它指人類食用昆蟲；末句則把 snails 排除在昆蟲之外， 說牠們是 molluscs。只看首尾句，可以估計這段主要在建立文章話題和作者態度：作者知道有些生物，例如蝸牛，已被某些文化視為美食，但他想討論的焦點是「真正的昆蟲」，並帶有一點抗拒和幽默語氣。"},{"number":2,"summary":"首句明確定義 true insects：六條腿、三個身體部分、硬外骨骼和兩條觸角；末句引用 Peter Ferguson，指出世界正面對餵養人口的困難，卻忽略大量昆蟲資源，這不合邏輯。只看首尾句，可以估計這段先劃定昆蟲範圍，再引入 Peter 的支持觀點：昆蟲數量龐大、熱量品質高，也可能成為食物問題的生態解法。"},{"number":3,"summary":"首句說西方文化確實忽略昆蟲，因為長期有更好的替代肉類；末句轉到 Thailand 市場，說 locusts / grasshoppers 常被油炸成一堆出售。只看首尾句，可以判斷這段主要比較西方和其他文化。西方依賴畜牧肉類，但 Africa、Asia、Oceania 等地早有食蟲傳統，並列出許多昆蟲及 arachnids 作食物例子。"},{"number":4,"summary":"首句要求讀者考慮 African mopane worm；末句說野生 mopane worms 的採收和銷售已成為 multimillion-dollar industry，養活數百萬人，主要是 indigenous Africans。只看首尾句，可以估計這段用 mopane worm 作具體案例，說明某些昆蟲食物如何被採集、處理、罐裝、出售，並具有真實經濟和糧食價值。"},{"number":5,"summary":"首句說 Peter 正熱情解釋他為何吃昆蟲；末句總結昆蟲 cheap to buy、cheap to breed、easy to manage。只看首尾句，可以估計這段集中呈現 Peter 的正面論點：昆蟲有蛋白質、維他命、礦物質和脂肪，也有 calcium、iron、zinc、copper 等營養；同時牠們在環保和飼養效率上比 cattle 更有優勢。"},{"number":6,"summary":"首句說昆蟲繁殖速度驚人，這一點難以反駁；末句提醒在密集 pesticide 使用或農地 commercial spraying 後收集的昆蟲不應食用。只看首尾句，可以估計這段先承認昆蟲作食物的生產效率，再補充安全風險。重點包括繁殖快、轉化成食物速度高、用地用水少，但也要注意 parasites、 pesticides、toxins 和 allergic reactions。"},{"number":7,"summary":"首句直接問 taste，即昆蟲味道如何；末句引用 Peter，說人類其實已經是 insectivores，只需再踏出下一個 logical step。只看首尾句，可以判斷結尾段轉向心理接受問題。Peter 承認 taste 需要習慣，但他指出人類早已在不知不覺中吃下昆蟲碎片、幼蟲和排泄物，例如吃 rice 時可能吃到 rice-weevil larvae。 Questions 1–4：TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN"}]},"questions":[{"number":1,"answer":"FALSE","answerKey":"FALSE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“The French are well known for eating insects.”","translation":"法國人以食用昆蟲聞名。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題要判斷 “The French” 和 “eating insects” 是否被原文連在一起。題目中的強定位詞是 French 和 insects。重點不只在法國人有沒有吃某種小型生物，還要確認該生物是否屬於 insects。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 1"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“There is a formal word for it: entomophagy.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這件事有一個正式詞語：entomophagy，即食蟲行為。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“They are molluscs, and I’d like to think that makes a difference.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"牠們是軟體動物，而我願意相信這一點是有分別的。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以先估 Paragraph 1 會介紹 “eating insects” 這個主題，同時區分昆蟲和其他可食小動物。最後一句的 molluscs 對這題尤其重要，因為它暗示某種被提到的食物不屬於昆蟲。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目中最有定位力的字是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“The French” “insects”"},{"kind":"label","text":"掃描 Paragraph 1，可以找到"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“snails, those slimy garden pests, are relished as gourmet food, most famously by the French…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"蝸牛，那些黏滑的花園害蟲，被視為美食，最著名的例子是法國人喜歡吃牠們。"},{"kind":"label","text":"接著原文馬上補充"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“But, I counter, snails are not insects.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"但我反駁說，蝸牛並非昆蟲。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文把法國人和 snails 連在一起，沒有把法國人和 insects 連在一起。句子中的 “most famously by the French” 修飾的是 “snails … are relished as gourmet food”。也就是說，法國人以吃蝸牛聞名。"},{"kind":"label","text":"真正定案的是下一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“But, I counter, snails are not insects. They are molluscs…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"但我反駁說，蝸牛並非昆蟲。牠們是軟體動物。"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目命題"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"French are well known for eating insects."},{"kind":"label","text":"原文命題"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"French are well known for eating snails, and snails are molluscs, not insects."},{"kind":"label","text":"比較結果"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目把 snails 改成 insects，核心分類錯誤。因此答案是 FALSE。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義／反向關係","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“well known for eating insects”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“snails … are relished as gourmet food, most famously by the French” “snails are not insects” “They are molluscs”"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"最容易誤選 TRUE 的地方是 “most famously by the French”。這個短語確實說法國人因吃某種東西出名，但那種東西是 snails。IELTS 這類題常把相鄰資訊換成另一個類別，細讀時要檢查名詞分類是否一致。"}]}]},{"number":2,"answer":"TRUE","answerKey":"TRUE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Peter Ferguson is a nature-friendly person.”","translation":"Peter Ferguson 是一位重視自然、環境友善的人。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題要判斷人物描述是否和原文一致。定位詞非常明顯：Peter Ferguson。題目中的 “nature-friendly” 可能不會逐字出現，應留意 ecologically friendly、environmentally friendly 這類近義表達。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 2"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“What I’m talking about is eating true insects, those with six legs, three body parts, a hard exoskeleton, and two antennae.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我所說的是食用真正的昆蟲，也就是有六條腿、三個身體部分、硬外骨骼和兩條觸角的生物。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In a world having trouble feeding itself, that doesn’t make sense.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"在一個難以餵飽自己的世界中，這樣做並不合理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以先估 Paragraph 2 會從昆蟲定義走向昆蟲作為食物資源的合理性。這段也引入支持食蟲的人物。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目中最強定位詞是 “Peter Ferguson”。Paragraph 2 中有："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“…until I met a personable and ecologically friendly young man, Peter Ferguson…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"直到我遇見一位討人喜歡、具生態友善意識的年輕人 Peter Ferguson……"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文用 “ecologically friendly” 描述 Peter。ecological 指生態的；friendly 在這裡表示友善、支持、 重視。題目用 “nature-friendly” 作概括，意思非常接近。"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目命題"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Peter Ferguson is nature-friendly."},{"kind":"label","text":"原文命題"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Peter Ferguson is “ecologically friendly”."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"兩者方向一致，所以答案是 TRUE。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“nature-friendly”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“ecologically friendly”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫類型"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"直接近義詞。nature 和 ecology 都指自然環境、生態系統；friendly 表示態度友善或支持。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題較直接。需要留意的是，Peter 的主要角色是 advocate insects as culinary delight，但題目問的是人物特質，不是他是否 chef 或 scientist。看到人名後，要先找形容他的詞，而非立刻跳到他後面關於昆蟲的長篇理由。"}]}]},{"number":3,"answer":"FALSE","answerKey":"FALSE","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Human consumption of insects is a modern phenomenon.”","translation":"人類食用昆蟲是一種現代現象。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題的控制詞是 “modern phenomenon”。要找文章是否說食蟲是新近出現，還是有很長歷史。定位詞可以用 “history”、“long”、“Bible”、“cultures” 這類時間或文化訊號。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 3"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Ignore them we do, at least in Western culture, where we have long had much better alternatives.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我們確實忽略昆蟲，至少在西方文化中如此，因為我們長期有更好的替代選擇。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“These same insects, incidentally, are commonly eaten in Thailand, where a visit to a local market will reveal multitudes of them, deep-fried in glistening piles for the delectation of passing shoppers.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"順帶一提，這些同類昆蟲在泰國也很常被食用；到當地市場一看，就會看到大量昆蟲被炸成閃亮的一堆，供路過顧客享用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計 Paragraph 3 會比較西方和非西方文化對昆蟲食物的不同態度。首句說西方長期有替代品；最後一句舉 Thailand 作現行例子。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目定位詞是 “modern phenomenon”。原文未必用 modern，但會用相反概念 “long history”。"},{"kind":"label","text":"Paragraph 3 中可以找到"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In Africa and Asia and among aboriginal or ethnic groups in Oceania, insects have an equally long history as an important dietary supplement.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"在非洲和亞洲，以及大洋洲的原住民或族群之中，昆蟲作為重要膳食補充品同樣有悠久歷史。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"原文的核心短語是 “an equally long history”。這直接否定 “modern phenomenon”。如果某種飲食有悠久歷史，它就不能被描述為現代才出現的現象。"},{"kind":"label","text":"後文還補充宗教文本例子"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Even the Christian Bible states that John the Baptist lived on locusts and wild honey…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"甚至《聖經》也記載施洗約翰以蝗蟲和野蜜為食。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這進一步說明食蟲並非現代才出現。它至少在古老文本和多種文化中已有記載。"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目命題"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Human consumption of insects is modern."},{"kind":"label","text":"原文命題"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Insects have a long history as food in Africa, Asia, Oceania, and even appear in the Christian Bible."},{"kind":"label","text":"比較結果"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"時間方向相反，所以答案是 FALSE。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義／反向關係","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“modern phenomenon”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“an equally long history” “Even the Christian Bible states…”"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Paragraph 2 的 Peter Ferguson 看似提出新穎、環保的食蟲觀點，學生可能因此覺得食蟲是現代"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"主張。可是 Paragraph 3 清楚說很多文化早有食蟲傳統。要分清「現代人重新倡議」和「食蟲行為本身的歷史」。"}]}]},{"number":4,"answer":"NOT GIVEN","answerKey":"NOT GIVEN","type":"TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN","prompt":"“Some insects are used for religious purposes.”","translation":"有些昆蟲被用於宗教用途。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題的定位詞是 “religious purposes”。文章中最接近宗教的線索是 “Christian Bible” 和 “John the Baptist”。但題目問的是昆蟲是否被用於宗教用途，例如儀式、祭祀、宗教象徵功能；要看原文有沒有這層資訊。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 3"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Ignore them we do, at least in Western culture, where we have long had much better alternatives.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我們確實忽略昆蟲，至少在西方文化中如此，因為我們長期有更好的替代選擇。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“These same insects, incidentally, are commonly eaten in Thailand, where a visit to a local market will reveal multitudes of them, deep-fried in glistening piles for the delectation of passing shoppers.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"順帶一提，這些同類昆蟲在泰國很常被食用；到當地市場一看，就會看到大量昆蟲被炸成閃亮的一堆，供路過顧客享用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計這段重點是不同文化中的昆蟲食用習慣。它的方向偏向 food history 和 dietary supplement，不太像宗教儀式。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目最有定位力的是 “religious”。原文沒有 religious purposes，但有："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Even the Christian Bible states that John the Baptist lived on locusts and wild honey, locusts being grasshoppers in their swarming stage.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"甚至《聖經》也記載施洗約翰以蝗蟲和野蜜為食；蝗蟲就是群飛階段的 grasshoppers。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句提供的是一個食用昆蟲的歷史／文化例子。它說 John the Baptist “lived on” locusts and wild honey。“lived on” 表示以某物維生、作為食物來源。句中沒有說 locusts 被用於 worship、 ritual、ceremony、sacrifice 或 religious symbol。"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目需要的證據是"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"some insects are used for religious purposes."},{"kind":"label","text":"原文實際提供的是"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"a religious text mentions a religious figure eating locusts as food."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這兩者有關聯，但關係不夠。出現在宗教文本中，不等於昆蟲具有宗教用途。原文也沒有說昆蟲沒有宗教用途，所以不能選 FALSE。核心資料缺失，答案是 NOT GIVEN。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義／缺失關係","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“used for religious purposes”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“the Christian Bible states…” “John the Baptist lived on locusts and wild honey”"},{"kind":"label","text":"缺失部分"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"religious ritual religious ceremony religious symbolic use 祭祀或儀式用途"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"最大中伏位是 “Christian Bible”。學生看到宗教文本，容易把它連到 religious purposes。細讀時要看昆蟲在句中的功能：locusts 是 John the Baptist 的食物，不是宗教用品。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Questions 5–10：Table Completion"}]}]},{"number":5,"answer":"calcium","answerKey":"calcium","type":"Table Completion","prompt":"grasshoppers — contain 5 _________________","translation":"grasshoppers 含有 ______。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這是 Table Completion。空格前是 “contain”，所以答案需要是營養物質名詞，且不可超過 TWO WORDS。定位詞是 grasshoppers。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 5"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Peter is enthusiastically telling me why he does it.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Peter 正熱情地告訴我他為甚麼這樣做。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Insects are cheap to buy, cheap to breed, and easy to manage.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"昆蟲購買便宜、繁殖成本低，也容易管理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計 Paragraph 5 集中講 Peter 支持吃昆蟲的理由，包括營養、環保、成本和飼養效率。grasshopper 的營養資料很可能在這段。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目定位詞是 “grasshoppers”。原文出現："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“When I remain sceptical, Peter holds up a fried grasshopper. ‘This has lots of calcium.’”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"當我仍然懷疑時，Peter 拿起一隻炸 grasshopper。「這有很多 calcium。」"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"“this” 指前面的 “a fried grasshopper”。Peter 說 “This has lots of calcium”，所以 grasshoppers contain calcium。"}]},{"id":"answer-form","title":"答案形式檢查","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"calcium = 1 word 符合 NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS 詞性是名詞，能接在 contain 後面"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“contain”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“has lots of”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案：calcium。"}]}]},{"number":6,"answer":"Thailand","answerKey":"Thailand","type":"Table Completion","prompt":"grasshoppers — popular in 6 _________________","translation":"grasshoppers 在 ______ 受歡迎／常被食用。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"空格前是 “popular in”，答案需要是地方名。定位詞仍是 grasshoppers，但原文可能使用 locusts，因為文章解釋 locusts 是 grasshoppers 的 swarming stage。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 3"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Ignore them we do, at least in Western culture, where we have long had much better alternatives.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我們確實忽略昆蟲，至少在西方文化中如此，因為我們長期有更好的替代選擇。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“These same insects, incidentally, are commonly eaten in Thailand, where a visit to a local market will reveal multitudes of them, deep-fried in glistening piles for the delectation of passing shoppers.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"順帶一提，這些同類昆蟲在 Thailand 很常被食用；到當地市場一看，就會看到大量昆蟲被炸成閃亮的一堆，供路過顧客享用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計這段會講不同地方食用昆蟲的習慣。最後一句已經出現 Thailand 和 commonly eaten。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目用 grasshoppers。原文先說："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“locusts being grasshoppers in their swarming stage.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"locusts 就是群飛階段的 grasshoppers。"},{"kind":"label","text":"下一句說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“These same insects… are commonly eaten in Thailand…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這些同類昆蟲在 Thailand 很常被食用。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"這裡要連起兩步"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"locusts = grasshoppers in their swarming stage these same insects are commonly eaten in Thailand"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"所以表格中的 grasshoppers popular in 的答案是 Thailand。"}]},{"id":"answer-form","title":"答案形式檢查","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thailand = 1 word 地名符合空格前 “popular in”"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“popular in”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“commonly eaten in”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案：Thailand。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"不要填 “Christian Bible” 或 “John the Baptist”。那一處只是說 locusts 在《聖經》中被提及為食物； 表格問地點，所以要看後面 “Thailand”。"}]}]},{"number":7,"answer":"indigenous Africans","answerKey":"indigenous Africans","type":"Table Completion","prompt":"mopane worms — primarily eaten by 7 _________________","translation":"mopane worms 主要由 ______ 食用。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"空格前是 “eaten by”，答案需要是人群。定位詞是 mopane worms，通常會回到 Paragraph 4 的例子。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 4"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Consider the African mopane worm, for example.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"例如，看看 African mopane worm。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“The harvest and sale of wild mopane worms is now a multimillion-dollar industry, feeding millions of people, mostly indigenous Africans.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"野生 mopane worms 的採收和銷售現在已是價值數百萬美元的產業，養活數百萬人，其中大多數是 indigenous Africans。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以判斷這段專門講 mopane worms。最後一句直接提到食用／依賴人群。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目定位詞是 “mopane worms” 和 “primarily eaten by”。原文未必用 primarily，但有 “mostly”："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“feeding millions of people, mostly indigenous Africans.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"養活數百萬人，其中大多數是 indigenous Africans。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"“mostly” 對應題目 “primarily”。“feeding millions of people” 表示這些 worms 作為食物養活很多人。人群是 “indigenous Africans”。"}]},{"id":"answer-form","title":"答案形式檢查","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"indigenous Africans = 2 words 符合 NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS 可放入 “primarily eaten by indigenous Africans”"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“primarily”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“mostly”"},{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“eaten by”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“feeding”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案：indigenous Africans。"}]}]},{"number":8,"answer":"mopane leaves","answerKey":"mopane leaves","type":"Table Completion","prompt":"mopane worms — eat 8 _________________","translation":"mopane worms 吃 ______。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"空格前是 eat，需要食物名詞。定位詞是 mopane worms。注意文章在 Paragraph 4 講人吃 mopane worms，在 Paragraph 5 講 worms 吃甚麼，所以要跨段掃描。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 5"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Peter is enthusiastically telling me why he does it.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Peter 正熱情地告訴我他為甚麼這樣做。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Insects are cheap to buy, cheap to breed, and easy to manage.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"昆蟲購買便宜、繁殖成本低，也容易管理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計這段會講昆蟲作食物的優點，尤其是營養和飼養效率。mopane worm 的食物轉化率可能在這段。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目定位詞是 “mopane worms” 和 “eat”。Paragraph 5 中 Peter 說："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Three kilograms of mopane leaves will feed a kilogram of worms—a 30 per cent payback.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"三公斤 mopane leaves 可以養出一公斤 worms，回報率是 30%。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這句的主體是 “Three kilograms of mopane leaves”。動詞是 “will feed”。對象是 “a kilogram of worms”。這表示 mopane worms 吃 mopane leaves。"}]},{"id":"answer-form","title":"答案形式檢查","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"mopane leaves = 2 words 符合 NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS 放入表格：mopane worms eat mopane leaves"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“eat”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“will feed”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案：mopane leaves。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"不要填 “worms”。句子是 “leaves feed worms”，不是 worms feed leaves。Completion 題要看主語和受詞，避免把方向倒轉。"}]}]},{"number":9,"answer":"southern China","answerKey":"southern China","type":"Table Completion","prompt":"scorpions — are popular in 9 _________________","translation":"scorpions 在 ______ 受歡迎／被視為美食。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"空格前是 “popular in”，答案需要地點。定位詞是 scorpions。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 3"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Ignore them we do, at least in Western culture, where we have long had much better alternatives.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我們確實忽略昆蟲，至少在西方文化中如此，因為我們長期有更好的替代選擇。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“These same insects, incidentally, are commonly eaten in Thailand, where a visit to a local market will reveal multitudes of them, deep-fried in glistening piles for the delectation of passing shoppers.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"順帶一提，這些同類昆蟲在 Thailand 很常被食用；到當地市場一看，就會看到大量昆蟲被炸成閃亮的一堆，供路過顧客享用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計這段列出不同文化中的可食昆蟲和類似生物。scorpions 的地點應在中間例子列表中。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目定位詞是 “scorpions”。原文說："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“scorpions (a delicacy in southern China)”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"scorpions，在 southern China 被視為美味佳餚。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"“a delicacy” 表示美食、珍饈，對應表格的 “are popular”。地點是 “southern China”。"}]},{"id":"answer-form","title":"答案形式檢查","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"southern China = 2 words 符合 NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS 可放入 “are popular in southern China”"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“are popular”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“a delicacy”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案：southern China。"}]}]},{"number":10,"answer":"arachnids","answerKey":"arachnids","type":"Table Completion","prompt":"scorpions — are a type of 10 _________________","translation":"scorpions 是一種 ______。","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"空格前是 “a type of”，答案需要分類名詞。定位詞是 scorpions。這題要回到文章早段的生物分類。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 2"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“What I’m talking about is eating true insects, those with six legs, three body parts, a hard exoskeleton, and two antennae.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我所說的是食用真正的昆蟲，也就是有六條腿、三個身體部分、硬外骨骼和兩條觸角的生物。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In a world having trouble feeding itself, that doesn’t make sense.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"在一個難以餵飽自己的世界中，這樣做並不合理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計這段先定義 insects，再擴大可討論範圍，最後引入食蟲的生態和糧食理由。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目定位詞是 “scorpions”。Paragraph 2 有："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“We can extend this definition to our eight-legged arachnids (spiders and scorpions), as well.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"我們也可以把這個定義延伸到八條腿的 arachnids，例如 spiders 和 scorpions。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"括號中 “spiders and scorpions” 是 arachnids 的例子。題目問 scorpions are a type of what，所以答案是 arachnids。"}]},{"id":"answer-form","title":"答案形式檢查","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"arachnids = 1 word 符合 NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS 分類名詞，文法自然"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"題目"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“are a type of”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“arachnids (spiders and scorpions)”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"答案：arachnids。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"scorpions 出現在 Paragraph 3 的食物例子中，也出現在 Paragraph 2 的分類定義中。Question 9 問地點，所以用 Paragraph 3；Question 10 問分類，所以要回到 Paragraph 2。相同定位詞會因空格功能不同而定位到不同段落。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Questions 11–13：Multiple Choice"}]}]},{"number":11,"answer":"D — are usually treated before being eaten","answerKey":"D","type":"Multiple Choice","prompt":"“Mopane worms…”","translation":"關於 mopane worms，哪一項正確？","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這是 Multiple Choice。定位詞是 Mopane worms。四個選項分別涉及名稱、成長階段、商業飼養、 食用前處理。要逐項核對 Paragraph 4。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 4"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Consider the African mopane worm, for example.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"例如，看看 African mopane worm。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“The harvest and sale of wild mopane worms is now a multimillion-dollar industry, feeding millions of people, mostly indigenous Africans.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"野生 mopane worms 的採收和銷售現在已是價值數百萬美元的產業，養活數百萬人，其中大多數是 indigenous Africans。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計 Paragraph 4 會完整介紹 mopane worm，包括牠是甚麼、如何取得、如何食用和經濟價值。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用題目詞定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"題目主體 “Mopane worms” 直接定位到 Paragraph 4。選項中的關鍵詞可逐一掃描："},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"appropriately named moth form raised for profit treated before eaten"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文中最相關的句子是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“To begin with, the name is a misnomer.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"首先，這個名稱本身是一個誤稱。"},{"kind":"label","text":"以及"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“The hairy yellow-striped creatures are eagerly sought after, hand-picked from trees in the wild, pinched by the tail end to squeeze out the slimy green intestinal tract, after which they are usually sun-dried or smoked and are then ready for consumption.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這些有毛、帶黃色條紋的生物很受追捧，人們從野外樹上手工採摘，捏住尾端擠出黏滑的綠色腸道，之後通常會曬乾或煙燻，然後便可食用。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"選項 D 說 “are usually treated before being eaten”。原文說牠們會被："},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"hand-picked pinched by the tail end squeezed out the intestinal tract usually sun-dried or smoked then ready for consumption"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這整個過程就是食用前處理。尤其 “usually sun-dried or smoked” 直接支持 “usually treated before being eaten”。"}]},{"id":"options","title":"選項分析","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A “are appropriately named.” 錯。原文說 “the name is a misnomer”，即名稱不準確。mopane worm 其實是 caterpillar，不是 worm。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"B “usually reach their moth form.” 錯。原文說牠最終會變成 moth，但 “most never reach that stage”。多數未到 moth 階段便被採收。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"C “are extensively raised for profit.” 錯。原文說 “harvest and sale of wild mopane worms” 是大產業。wild 和 hand-picked from trees in the wild 表示採收野生 worms；選項加入 “raised”，即人工飼養，文章沒有支持。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"D “are usually treated before being eaten.” 正確。原文有擠出腸道、曬乾或煙燻等處理。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"選項 D"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“treated before being eaten”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“pinched… to squeeze out…” “usually sun-dried or smoked” “then ready for consumption”"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"C 最具迷惑性，因為原文確實說 multimillion-dollar industry。可是產業化不等於人工飼養。文章說的是 wild mopane worms 的採收和銷售，選項 C 把 “harvest and sale” 改成 “raised”，動作錯了。"}]}]},{"number":12,"answer":"A — multiply quickly","answerKey":"A","type":"Multiple Choice","prompt":"“Insects…”","translation":"關於昆蟲，哪一項正確？","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題是 Multiple Choice，主體很廣：Insects。四個選項分別涉及繁殖速度、生食、安全性、溫室氣體。最直接的定位段落是 Paragraph 6，因為它集中講昆蟲繁殖和安全問題。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 6"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“One can’t argue with that.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這一點很難反駁。"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Insects collected after intensive pesticide use or commercial spraying of local agricultural land should, of course, not be eaten.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"當然，在密集使用 pesticide 或本地農地 commercial spraying 後收集的昆蟲不應食用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計 Paragraph 6 先承接 Peter 的昆蟲優勢，再在結尾補充安全限制。這段很適合判斷昆蟲的繁殖和食用安全。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用選項定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"選項 A 的定位詞是 multiply quickly。Paragraph 6 說："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“The phenomenal rate at which insects breed is well known…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"昆蟲繁殖的驚人速度是眾所周知的。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"選項 B 的定位詞是 raw。原文說："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“Cooking insects thoroughly is recommended.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"建議要把昆蟲徹底煮熟。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"選項 C 的定位詞是 safe。原文提到 parasites、pesticides、toxins、allergic reactions，沒有概括為 mostly safe。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"選項 D 的定位詞是 greenhouse gas。Paragraph 5 說 “Insects don’t produce greenhouse gases”，不是 “produce small amounts”。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"正確答案 A 的證據是"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“The phenomenal rate at which insects breed is well known, and more than makes up for their small size.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"昆蟲繁殖的驚人速度是眾所周知的，而且這足以彌補牠們體型細小的不足。"},{"kind":"label","text":"後面例子進一步說"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“A female cricket might be a fraction of the weight of a huge beef cow, but lays up to 1,500 eggs a month…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"一隻雌性 cricket 的重量可能只是巨大肉牛的一小部分，但每月最多可產 1,500 顆卵。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這直接支持 “multiply quickly”。"}]},{"id":"options","title":"選項分析","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A “multiply quickly.” 正確。對應 “phenomenal rate at which insects breed” 和 “lays up to 1,500 eggs a month”。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"B “are best eaten raw.” 錯。原文建議 “Cooking insects thoroughly”，方向相反。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"C “are mostly safe to eat.” 缺乏支持。原文說有寄生蟲、農藥、毒素和過敏反應風險，因此不能概括為 mostly safe。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"D “produce small amounts of greenhouse gas.” 原文中 Peter 的說法是 “Insects don’t produce greenhouse gases”。即使現實中可再討論，這篇文章的文字不支持 “small amounts”。"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"選項 A"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“multiply quickly”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“phenomenal rate at which insects breed” “lays up to 1,500 eggs a month”"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"D 會吸引人，因為 greenhouse gases 確實在文章中出現。不過原文的語氣是 “don’t produce”， 選項改成 “produce small amounts”。IELTS MCQ 要按文章字面和語氣，不可用外部常識調整答案。"}]}]},{"number":13,"answer":"D — probably eats rice weevil larvae","answerKey":"D","type":"Multiple Choice","prompt":"“The author…”","translation":"關於作者，哪一項正確？","sections":[{"id":"task","title":"題型與判斷任務","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"這題問 author 本人，不是 Peter 的觀點，也不是一般人。選項要回到第一人稱線索，例如 “as I do”、“my example”、“I remain sceptical”。目標段落是 Paragraph 7。"}]},{"id":"skim","title":"Skim：先看段落功能","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"目標段落：Paragraph 7"},{"kind":"label","text":"第一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“But what about the taste?”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"但味道又如何呢？"},{"kind":"label","text":"最後一句"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“In that sense, we’re already insectivores. We’ve just got to take the next logical step.”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"從這個意義上說，我們已經是食蟲者。我們只需要踏出下一個合乎邏輯的步驟。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"只看首尾句，可以估計結尾段處理 taste 和心理接受問題。它也會談到人類已在無意中吃昆蟲， 這和作者個人可能吃到甚麼有關。"}]},{"id":"scan","title":"Scan：用選項定位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"四個選項中，D 的 “rice weevil larvae” 是最強定位詞。Paragraph 7 有："},{"kind":"quote","text":"“For example, most people who eat rice (as I do) inadvertently consume more than a few rice-weevil larvae…”"},{"kind":"label","text":"中文意思"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"例如，大多數吃米飯的人，也包括我，都會在無意中吃下不少 rice-weevil larvae。"}]},{"id":"read","title":"Read：細讀答案句","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"關鍵是括號中的 “as I do”。它清楚說作者自己也吃 rice。原文主句說 “most people who eat rice … inadvertently consume more than a few rice-weevil larvae”。把兩者連起來："},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"作者吃 rice。 大多數吃 rice 的人會無意中吃到 rice-weevil larvae。 所以作者 probably eats rice-weevil larvae。"}]},{"id":"options","title":"選項分析","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A “likes snails.” 原文只說 snails 被法國人視為美食；作者還刻意把 snails 排除在 insects 之外。沒有說作者喜歡 snails。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"B “probably eats mopane worms.” 作者提到 “my mopane worm example”，但那是他討論的例子，沒有說他吃過或常吃。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"C “believes insects can taste good.”"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Paragraph 7 中 Peter 對 taste 的回答是 “You get used to it.” 作者則 “nod sceptically”，顯示他仍"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"有保留。文章沒有說作者相信 insects taste good。"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"D “probably eats rice weevil larvae.” 正確。對應 “most people who eat rice (as I do) inadvertently consume…”"}]},{"id":"paraphrase","title":"同義改寫","blocks":[{"kind":"label","text":"選項 D"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“probably eats rice weevil larvae”"},{"kind":"label","text":"原文"},{"kind":"quote","text":"“most people who eat rice (as I do) inadvertently consume more than a few rice-weevil larvae”"},{"kind":"label","text":"改寫類型"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"由一般規律加上作者自我描述作短距離推論。"}]},{"id":"trap","title":"中伏位","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"B 的 “mopane worms” 容易令人誤會，因為作者說 “my mopane worm example”。這裡的 “my example” 表示他之前提出過這個例子，不表示他吃過 mopane worms。Q13 問作者個人，很重要的線索是括號中的 “as I do”。"}]}]}]}}});
